  "Number": 28,
  "Question": "If \\(2137^{753}\\) is multiplied out, the units’ digit in the final product is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1\\)",
    "B": "\\(3\\)",
    "C": "\\(5\\)",
    "D": "\\(7\\)",
    "E": "\\(9\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "A product’s units digit depends only on its factors’ units digits, since every other contribution is a multiple of 10. Thus we can follow powers of \\(7\\) instead of multiplying out powers of \\(2137\\).\n\nThe first four powers of \\(7\\) are \\(7,49,343,2401\\), with units digits\n\\[\n7,\\ 9,\\ 3,\\ 1.\n\\]\nMultiplying the last digit by \\(7\\) starts the same cycle again. Since\n\\[\n753=4\\cdot188+1,\n\\]\nthe requested power has the first units digit in the cycle. The answer is \\(7\\), choice D.",
